{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["The baobab, a genus of trees typical for arid areas, is known to be used by Indigenous Australians as a source of water, food and medical remedy. In the 1890s however, a large, hollow baobab located near Derby, Western Australia was adapted for what usage?","Prison"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"science-technology\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
